\section{Conclusion}
\label{sec:conclusion}

A recommended 3-prompt $\times$ 3-seed design reduces item requirements from 552 to 178 for $G \geq 0.80$, confirmed across five benchmarks under binary scoring; multi-facet designs minimize items when item construction is costly, while single-condition designs suit compute-constrained settings. All budgets assume binary scoring; extending to other model scales and continuous metrics is a priority. Code, data, and a D-study calculator will be released upon publication.

